invariant: INV-7
file: webpki_cfg.c
catches: webpki_session_aes_runtime
reason: an AES=runtime client whose caller's probe found no AES instructions
  admits a caller's cipher_suites list that names an AES-GCM suite, so
  its hello offers a suite the session cannot run on that CPU. The ruling
  refuses such a list at init rather than cutting it down
  (docs/decisions.md 81). test_webpki_runtime_without_aes requires
  ch_connect to refuse AES-128-GCM alone and ChaCha20 then AES-256-GCM
  before a byte leaves.

--- old
